dropped the body of system-header function
could not fully type-check
--
libstdc++ 13 <format>: std::format("{}", 42) makes the front end crash
(SIGSEGV, unbounded recursion in primary_base / vtable_pointer_component),
the root cause being cpp11_partial_specialization_const_T_matching_const_array
(incrementable_traits<const char[1]>).  Including <format> alone drops
format:1422 'format', 2456 _M_write, 3759/3765 vformat_to and
bits/ranges_algobase.h:311 operator() (also seen in cpp20_format_header).
3759/3765 and 2456 are
cpp_function_template_default_argument_on_earlier_declaration; 1422 and 311
are being reduced.  g++ 13 accepts this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
